{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request 13349afa, identifiers (c+d): the entry records each\nkind that varies, a fixed place needs no member, and the caller record\nis withdrawn.\n\n1. Delivery and genesis. Approved as you propose. Every delivery input\n   has a required `sourceKind`, a ScopeKind. A genesis input has\n   `sourceKind: null` if and only if `source` is null. The scope\n   writes it from the checked genesis of the source, before the\n   prospective `artroom-input-1` digest. The confirmation draft and the\n   result callback carry the same value. The changed input hashes,\n   entry hashes and descendant causes are accepted: the cutover makes\n   a new format. No seed member.\n2. Named fact use. `FactUse` gains the matched checked kind beside\n   `fact` and `content`. Approved.\n3. Grant observation and creation-context membership. No new member.\n   The contract fixes the kind of each place: the `of` of a grant's\n   `ObservationUse`, and `genesis.message.body.membership`, name a\n   Membership. The scope checks the genesis of that sequence when it\n   reads it (site 2d of ruling 429c1be7). The place is the record. A\n   constant in every act entry adds bytes and no information. If the\n   contract lets either place name another kind, stop and say so.\n4. The comparison with an actual genesis covers the separately carried\n   source too, as peer finding F1 says, and not only `context.facts`.\n5. Replay. With the verified genesis of a sequence in its permitted\n   input, Replay compares it with the recorded kind or with the fixed\n   place. A difference is a mismatch. Without that genesis, Replay\n   judges with the recorded kind or the place. One row of `TRUSTS`\n   says: the kind that an entry records, or that its place fixes, for\n   a sequence whose genesis Replay did not read. No kind gives a pin,\n   an `under`, a Native admission, a CheckedSequence, a `#runs` entry\n   or `#proven` as `replayed`. The witness of 608503ab item 4 stays: a\n   handler that declares `from.pin`, over a sender known only by a\n   recorded kind, stops `incomplete`.\n\nWithdrawn. The caller record of ruling 70186a25, items 1 to 5, and\nitems 2, 3 and 5 of 608503ab. No caller states a kind. The report has\nno list of records. A caller anchor is an exact fact, as today.\n`--trust-published-anchors` supplies anchors alone, and the published\nlist holds no kind. The exporter keeps its limit of anchors to\nRegister and Membership sequences from its own checked birth read. The\nmanifest row and the finite catalog give the retained definition name\nas today, and the `anchors` row of `TRUSTS` keeps its words. Remove the\ncaller-record plumbing from the offline branch.\n\nSection 8 of the note. In \"References\", the two sentences become: \"A\nlive handler that tests the kind of the sender reads the genesis of\nthe source scope. The receiver reads that genesis once and records the\nkind in the entry.\" This paragraph replaces the one of 70186a25:\n\n  **The kind of another sequence.** A reference holds no kind, because\n  the kind is in the seed. A scope checks the kind against the genesis\n  of the sequence when it takes a delivery, when it is created from a\n  source, when it reads a named fact and when it reads a grant. The\n  entry then holds the kind: `sourceKind` beside the source of a\n  delivery or of a genesis, and `kind` in each fact use. A grant and a\n  creation context name a Membership by their place. A later judgment\n  of the scope reads the entry and reads no other scope. Replay\n  compares the recorded kind with the genesis when its permitted input\n  holds that genesis. Otherwise it judges with the recorded kind, and\n  its report says so.\n\nRulings 79439167 (cache), 429c1be7 (lookup follows a read), 33c2c7c7\n(archive Rules root) and 34774677 stand. The checker reads this ruling\nas it read 70186a25. Source work on items 1 and 2 may go on meanwhile.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}